From 3dc2b59945aa49a86cb457ebad5881fe6aa579e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:59:35 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Module dependency scans are memoized on fully observed
 inputs

Dependency scans use the exact request buffers, and a scan is reused only after every observed input (files, negative queries, builtin expansions such as __DATE__) replays unchanged. Complete inputs are hashed with BLAKE3, observations are bounded and indexed, identical publications are coordinated, fully observed semantic failures are reused, and hosts without native admission keep complete-content controls.

* fix(modules): dependency scans use exact request buffers

  Project-module scanners used the compilation database filesystem even
  when prerequisite construction received a request filesystem. Rebind
  production facades to request views, overlay exact captured main contents,
  and compare current imports before reusing completion prerequisites.

  Keep overlay bytes in request-owned immutable storage: dependency scanning
  caches borrowed VFS buffers across temporary worker views. Per-view copies
  otherwise leave dangling buffers during subsequent provider scans.

  Remove the disk-only buildability verdict memo until every scan/provider
  input can be validated. Regression evidence covers exact unsaved contents,
  supplied filesystem precedence, and the module DAG/recovery raw suite.
  Bounded verified-input scan reuse is a separate follow-up.

* perf(clangd): successful module scans replay all observed inputs before reuse

  Fresh scanner services expose successful and negative filesystem observations. Replay exact bytes, metadata, alias relationships, directory prefixes and environment before reuse or publication. Bound live memo ownership across concurrent validators, and decline unknown response provenance or unsupported observations.

* Observe actual time-dependent builtin expansions before caching module scans

* [clangd] Reuse fully observed semantic module scan failures

  Preserve diagnostics without publishing failed providers; revalidate exact request inputs and cancellation. Observe real paths and compact only identical idempotent facts while retaining ordered directory operations. Bound complete manifests to 8192 facts under the existing shared 32 MiB metadata budget.

  Consolidates preserved commits 0aa9f31a5 and its cancellation follow-up.

* [clangd] Bound coordination of identical scan cache publications

* [clangd] Bound and index exact dependency scan observations

* [clangd] Hash complete scan inputs with LLVM BLAKE3

* [clangd] Test scan publication within native driver admission

* [clangd] Keep complete-content scan controls on unsupported native hosts
